<https://github.com/john1hsu/ai-knowledge-graph/id/least-to-most-prompting> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A few-shot prompting technique that first asks a language model to break a hard problem into a sequence of simpler subproblems, then solves those subproblems in order, feeding each earlier answer into the prompt for the next, so the model can generalise to problems harder than its exemplars." .
