<https://github.com/john1hsu/ai-knowledge-graph/id/quantization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A model-compression technique that represents a neural network's weights (and often its activations) with low-precision numbers such as 8-bit or 4-bit integers or 8/4-bit floats instead of 16- or 32-bit floats, cutting memory and bandwidth and enabling faster integer or low-precision arithmetic at a small cost in accuracy." .
